# .superpowers/ is agent scratch — BUT the per-task ledgers (progress.md, briefs, reports) are the
# synthesized "why" behind every ruling, fix round, and accepted residual in this project, and they
# cannot be re-derived at any price. Those .md files are preserved in git (Lance, 2026-07-31:
# "Preserve all info"). Everything else here stays ignored: review .diff packages (regenerable from
# git via scripts/review-package) and artifacts/ (~959M of cached source payloads — re-fetchable,
# see docs/ARTIFACTS.md for the cost of doing so).
.superpowers/*
!.superpowers/sdd/
.superpowers/sdd/*
!.superpowers/sdd/*/
.superpowers/sdd/*/*
!.superpowers/sdd/**/*.md
!.superpowers/sdd/*.md
node_modules/
.playwright-mcp/

# Playwright snapshot artifacts written with --filename to repo root
*-resolved.yml

# Retraction manifests (scripts/find-misattributed-votes.mjs --out). Generated, ~228KB, and stale
# the moment the scheduler ticks — retract-misattributed-votes.mjs deliberately regenerates from
# the live database rather than reading one of these back, so a committed copy would only ever be
# a misleading snapshot.
# ANCHORED with a leading slash, deliberately. Unanchored, `manifest.json` matches that name at
# ANY depth — so the day anyone adds `site/manifest.json` (a PWA web app manifest is the obvious
# one for this site) git would silently refuse to track it, the file would never reach Cloudflare
# Pages, and the page would 404 for a manifest that exists locally and looks committed. The
# retraction manifests this rule targets are only ever written to the repo ROOT by
# `scripts/find-misattributed-votes.mjs --out`. (RapidForge registry, 2026-08-29: the `data/` trap.)
/manifest.json
/*-manifest.json
